/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator Compressed Air Reduction Calculator
 * @ingroup treasure_hunt_calculators
 * @brief Calculates annual compressed air consumption, energy use, and cost for compressed air reduction measures.
 * @details This calculator estimates annual compressed air consumption and associated energy use and
 * cost for compressed air reduction measures identified during an energy treasure hunt or efficiency
 * assessment. It supports four measurement methods for determining air flow or consumption, and two
 * utility types for translating consumption into a monetary cost.
 *
 * The calculation follows these steps for each measure:
 * 1. **Flow Meter** — Read flow rate directly from an installed meter, then multiply by operating
 *    time and the units multiplier to obtain annual consumption
 * 2. **Bag Method** — Compute flow rate from the bag volume and fill time, then multiply by operating
 *    time and both quantity multipliers (bags and units) to obtain annual consumption
 * 3. **Orifice/Pressure** — Compute single-nozzle flow rate from a quadratic nozzle equation using
 *    pre-calibrated coefficients, scale by the number of nozzles, then multiply by operating time
 *    to obtain annual consumption (units multiplier is not applied for this method)
 * 4. **Other** — Accept a directly supplied annual consumption value without further conversion
 * 5. **Compressed Air Utility** — Multiply consumption by the cost rate per unit volume to obtain
 *    annual energy cost; electrical energy use is not applicable
 * 6. **Electricity Utility** — Convert consumption to electrical energy use via the compressor
 *    specific power, then multiply by the electricity cost rate to obtain annual energy cost
 * 7. **Totals** — Sum energy use, energy cost, flow rate, and consumption across all measures
 *
 * Relevant formulas and symbol definitions are documented below.
 *
 * @heading{Flow Meter Consumption}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_reduction_flow_meter_formula
 *
 * @heading{Bag Method Flow Rate}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_reduction_bag_formula
 *
 * @heading{Orifice/Pressure Method Flow Rate}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_reduction_pressure_formula
 *
 * @heading{Electricity Energy Use}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_reduction_electricity_formula
 *
 * @heading{Energy Cost}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_reduction_cost_formula
 *
 * @heading{Nozzle Coefficient Reference}
 * @copydoc compressed_air_nozzle_coefficient_data
 */

/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_reduction_flow_meter_formula Flow Meter Consumption Formula
 * @ingroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator
 * @brief Annual compressed air consumption derived from a flow meter reading.
 * @details An installed flow meter provides an instantaneous flow rate reading. This is multiplied
 * by the annual operating time, a unit conversion factor of 60 (to convert hours to minutes), and
 * the quantity multiplier to obtain total annual consumption in standard cubic feet.
 *
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-flow-meter-consumption; C = Q_{meter} \cdot t_{op} \cdot 60 \cdot n}
 *
 * @subheading{Symbols}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{C; Annual compressed air consumption; \cubic\foot\per\year}
 * @symrow{Q_{meter}; Flow rate reading from the installed meter; \cubic\foot\per\minute}
 * @symrow{t_{op}; Annual operating hours; \hour\per\year}
 * @symrow{60; Unit conversion factor (minutes per hour); \minute\per\hour}
 * @symrow{n; Quantity multiplier (number of identical measures); \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 */

/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_reduction_bag_formula Bag Method Flow Rate and Consumption Formula
 * @ingroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator
 * @brief Compressed air flow rate and annual consumption estimated using the bag method.
 * @details The bag method estimates flow rate by measuring how long it takes to fill a
 * known-volume bag with compressed air from a leak or equipment vent. Dividing the bag volume
 * by the fill time (converted to minutes) gives the instantaneous flow rate in scfm. Annual
 * consumption is then computed from the flow rate, operating hours, and both quantity
 * multipliers: the number of bags tested simultaneously and the outer units multiplier.
 *
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-bag-flow-rate; Q_{bag} = \frac{V_{bag}}{t_{fill} / 60}}
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-bag-consumption; C = Q_{bag} \cdot t_{op} \cdot N_{bags} \cdot 60 \cdot n}
 *
 * @subheading{Symbols}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{Q_{bag}; Estimated compressed air flow rate; \cubic\foot\per\minute}
 * @symrow{V_{bag}; Internal volume of the bag; \cubic\foot}
 * @symrow{t_{fill}; Time to fill the bag with compressed air; \second}
 * @symrow{60; Unit conversion factor (seconds per minute); \second\per\minute}
 * @symrow{C; Annual compressed air consumption; \cubic\foot\per\year}
 * @symrow{t_{op}; Annual operating hours; \hour\per\year}
 * @symrow{N_{bags}; Number of bags tested simultaneously; \unitless}
 * @symrow{n; Outer quantity multiplier (number of identical measures); \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 */

/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_reduction_pressure_formula Orifice/Pressure Method Flow Rate Formula
 * @ingroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator
 * @brief Compressed air flow rate estimated from nozzle type and supply pressure.
 * @details The orifice/pressure method estimates flow rate using a quadratic equation fit to
 * empirical flow-versus-pressure data for 13 standard nozzle types (indices 0–12). Each nozzle
 * type has a distinct set of coefficients @math{a}, @math{b}, and @math{c} from the lookup table
 * in @ref compressed_air_nozzle_coefficients. The single-nozzle flow rate is computed from the
 * supply pressure; total flow rate and annual consumption then scale with the number of nozzles.
 * The outer units multiplier is not applied in this method.
 *
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-pressure-flow-rate; Q_{nozzle} = a \cdot P^2 + b \cdot P + c}
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-pressure-total-flow; Q_{total} = Q_{nozzle} \cdot N_{nozzles}}
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-pressure-consumption; C = Q_{total} \cdot t_{op} \cdot 60}
 *
 * @subheading{Symbols}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{Q_{nozzle}; Flow rate per individual nozzle; \cubic\foot\per\minute}
 * @symrow{a, b, c; Nozzle-type-specific quadratic coefficients (from lookup table); \unitless}
 * @symrow{P; Compressed air supply pressure; \psi}
 * @symrow{Q_{total}; Total compressed air flow rate; \cubic\foot\per\minute}
 * @symrow{N_{nozzles}; Number of nozzles in the system; \unitless}
 * @symrow{C; Annual compressed air consumption; \cubic\foot\per\year}
 * @symrow{t_{op}; Annual operating hours; \hour\per\year}
 * @symrow{60; Unit conversion factor (minutes per hour); \minute\per\hour}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * @note The coefficients @math{a}, @math{b}, and @math{c} depend entirely on the selected nozzle
 * type. All 13 nozzle-type coefficient sets are listed in @ref compressed_air_nozzle_coefficients.
 * @see compressed_air_nozzle_coefficients
 */ 
 
 
 /**
 * Electricity Energy Use Formula
 * @ingroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator
 * @brief Annual electrical energy use derived from compressed air consumption and compressor specific power.
 * @details When the electricity utility type is selected, the annual compressed air consumption is
 * converted to electrical energy use using the compressor specific power. The specific power
 * represents the electrical power required per unit of compressed air flow rate. Dividing by 60
 * converts the per-minute basis of the specific power to a per-hour basis consistent with the
 * consumption units.
 *
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-electricity; E = \frac{P_{specific}}{60} \cdot C}
 *
 * @subheading{Symbols}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{E; Annual electrical energy use; \kilo\watt\hour\per\year}
 * @symrow{P_{specific}; Compressor specific power (electrical power per unit flow rate); \kilo\watt\per\cubic\foot\per\minute}
 * @symrow{60; Unit conversion factor (minutes per hour); \minute\per\hour}
 * @symrow{C; Annual compressed air consumption; \cubic\foot\per\year}
 * @endsymtable
 */

/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_reduction_cost_formula Energy Cost Formula
 * @ingroup compressed_air_reduction_calculator
 * @brief Annual energy cost calculated from consumption or energy use and the applicable cost rate.
 * @details The cost calculation depends on the selected utility type. For the compressed air utility
 * type, annual cost is the product of consumption and the cost rate per unit volume. For the
 * electricity utility type, annual cost is the product of the electrical energy use and the
 * electricity cost rate.
 *
 * @subheading{Compressed Air Utility}
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-cost-air; C_{cost} = r_{air} \cdot C}
 *
 * @subheading{Electricity Utility}
 * @formula{compressed-air-reduction-cost-electricity; C_{cost} = r_{elec} \cdot E}
 *
 * @subheading{Symbols}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{C_{cost}; Annual energy cost; \dollar\per\year}
 * @symrow{r_{air}; Compressed air cost rate; \dollar\per\cubic\foot}
 * @symrow{C; Annual compressed air consumption; \cubic\foot\per\year}
 * @symrow{r_{elec}; Electricity cost rate; \dollar\per\kilo\watt\hour}
 * @symrow{E; Annual electrical energy use; \kilo\watt\hour\per\year}
 * @endsymtable
 */
